    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Be interested and open to the problems of others." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/518f18e2-c95c-4d41-9f01-6f244525326f> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Develop ideas for television and radio programs in accordance with the studio's policy." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/5192fe13-54d6-4635-acb7-9fa577065920> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Direct network and radio communications between different operational units. Receive and transfer further radio or telecom messages or calls. These might include messages from the public, or the emergency services." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/51b2dbdb-abaf-4f8e-9e02-56f822302876> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Repair computer code by analysing testing results, locating the defects causing the software to output an incorrect or unexpected result and remove these faults." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/5206b76c-ec88-4dab-b38a-2e8ec53b96f7> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Use the mastery of foreign languages orally or written in the tourism sector in order to communicate with collaborators or customers." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/521ea946-c58c-440f-95aa-983a7398c89a> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Inspect and amend the scenery and set-dressing to make sure the visual quality is optimal with in constraints of time, budget and manpower." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/52251ff9-43b8-43bd-a8cb-6b9950eff1e6> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Use specific software for data analysis, including statistics, spreadsheets, and databases. Explore possibilities in order to make reports to managers, superiors, or clients." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/52358f5d-b393-4db1-8bdb-ad7d61c83334> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Communicating with colleagues, clients and other outside groups to disseminate information on operational matters, problems and activities." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/5254d1be-0695-42b8-9132-e13580694ee9> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Adhere to assigned work schedule as prepared by the transportation company." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/5280aec9-9f9d-42cd-8c59-acb4b3479100> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Different musical styles and genres such as blues, jazz, reggae, rock, or indie." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/52be5108-726f-4291-82af-15fdd73174cd> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Command products from relevant suppliers to get convenient and profitable products to purchase." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/532e8a3a-d999-49cc-9945-e734f38beac0> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral """Audio-visual techniques and media production is the study of techniques and skills to produce books or newspapers, radio or TV production, film or video production, recorded music production and graphic reproduction. It includes programmes and qualifications in methods of colour reproduction, photography and computer graphics. Study of combining pictures, words and decorations in the production of books, magazines, posters, adverts etc. is also included.
Programmes and qualifications with the following main content are classified here:
Animation
Bookbinding
Camera operating
Compositing (printing)
Computer game production
Computer type-setting
Film and video production
Graphic design
Graphic reproduction
Illustration
Interactive media design
Media techniques
Multimedia production
Photography
Pre-press operations
Print finishing and binding
Printing
Publishing design, lay-out
Radio and TV production
Recorded music production
Sound techniques
Type-setting === Inclusions
Desktop publishing and lay-out are included here. === Exclusions
Programmes and qualifications in the use of specific software applications for desktop publishing and website development are excluded from this detailed field and included in detailed field 0611 'Computer use'.
Study of journalism (wording and content of messages) is excluded from this detailed field and included in detailed field 0321 'Journalism and reporting'.""" .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/53492232-4b49-4ea1-b5ef-a647bb11f886> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Compile data on inspections, patrols and security incidents into a report for management purposes." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/5350fa48-cc0c-45b7-8d4a-eb93ede80397> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Artificial intelligence engineer apply methods of artificial intelligence in engineering, robotics and computer science to design programs which simulate intelligence including thinking models, cognitive and knowledge-based systems, problem solving, and decision making. They also integrate structured knowledge into computer systems (ontologies, knowledge bases) in order to solve complex problems normally requiring a high level of human expertise or artificial intelligence methods." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/536b543a-b8e4-46ab-8cb8-e65468bda55a> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Update basic or integrated software included in devices, network components and embedded systems." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/536e8e10-25b3-4406-8785-7aaf180a4f5b> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Sound editors create the soundtrack and sound effects for motion pictures, television series or other multimedia productions. They are responsible for all the music and sound featured in the movie, series or videogames. Sound editors use equipment to edit and mix image and sound recordings and make sure that the music, sound and dialogue is synchronised with and fits in the scene. They work closely together with the video and motion picture editor." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/53a747a6-d074-469f-8c44-5500d7de38f3> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "Achieve objectives independently using optimal amount of time, effort, or cost." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/53e3fdcc-7b3d-4fc8-82bb-fb42b0e82a40> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "The computer language SQL is a query language for retrieval of information from a database and of documents containing the needed information. It is developed by the American National Standards Institute and the International Organization for Standardization." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/5417d4f7-84c6-476c-9a88-2bfca8a91bfb> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "The energy consumption and types of models of software as well as hardware elements." .

<http://data.europa.eu/esco/node-literal/5437f93d-5d1e-4be0-9ea4-d11c207c9c26> a esco:NodeLiteral ;
    esco:language "en"^^xsd:language ;
    esco:nodeLiteral "The offered waste and scrap products, their functionalities, properties and legal and regulatory requirements." .

